      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "Instructor: Welcome to another course module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 6.69,
          "en": "By now the basic should be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.69,
          "end": 9.78,
          "en": "and we had a closer look at what makes up an Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.78,
          "end": 13.74,
          "en": "Now chances are you already encountered your first error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.74,
          "end": 14.573,
          "en": "in your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.573,
          "end": 17.64,
          "en": "We even had some errors together in the apps we built.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.64,
          "end": 20.94,
          "en": "Now, fixing these errors is of course very important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.94,
          "end": 23.76,
          "en": "and not always straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 26.43,
          "en": "That is why in this section we're going to have a brief look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.43,
          "end": 27.51,
          "en": "at the tools we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.51,
          "end": 32.34,
          "en": "at our disposal for fixing errors in our Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.34,
          "end": 35.25,
          "en": "Here's a little example app attached to this lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.25,
          "end": 39.45,
          "en": "which looks nice but won't work as expected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.45,
          "end": 42.63,
          "en": "We are on our service dashboard, we could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.63,
          "end": 45.66,
          "en": "but if they click add server to add a new server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.66,
          "end": 46.77,
          "en": "watch what happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.77,
          "end": 48.09,
          "en": "We get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.09,
          "end": 51.72,
          "en": "Now you might get such errors a lot, and generally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.72,
          "end": 54.24,
          "en": "you might not always have your developer console open",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.24,
          "end": 56.487,
          "en": "though for developing, that's a good idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.487,
          "end": 59.85,
          "en": "But if something doesn't work the way you expect it to work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.85,
          "end": 62.37,
          "en": "like here when you click the button and nothing happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.37,
          "end": 64.5,
          "en": "opening the console, the developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.5,
          "end": 67.53,
          "en": "and their the JavaScript console is a great idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.53,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "Now here we clearly get an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 73.2,
          "en": "and error messages have gotten better in Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.2,
          "end": 76.68,
          "en": "So chances are the error message is indeed helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.68,
          "end": 78.45,
          "en": "So let's have a look at the error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.45,
          "end": 80.34,
          "en": "You should find it right at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.34,
          "end": 82.98,
          "en": "and here it says that in app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.98,
          "end": 85.68,
          "en": "That's the first important information piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.68,
          "end": 88.05,
          "en": "in the inline template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.05,
          "end": 89.91,
          "en": "Then this would be the line number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 89.91,
          "end": 92.16,
          "en": "and then the column where in the line.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 92.16,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "So line four.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 95.94,
          "en": "Now let's see if that is helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 95.94,
          "end": 97.62,
          "en": "That there the error was cost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 97.62,
          "end": 102.57,
          "en": "because we cannot read the property push of undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 102.57,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "Well, we get a couple of useful information pieces here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 109.74000000000001,
          "en": "So let's go to the app component then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.74000000000001,
          "end": 111.9,
          "en": "and let's have a look at it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 111.9,
          "end": 113.34,
          "en": "If we go there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.34,
          "end": 117.12,
          "en": "Well, the line four argument is only kind of helpful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 117.12,
          "end": 120.96,
          "en": "because line four is never the problematic core code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 120.96,
          "end": 123.78,
          "en": "in our template, nor in the TypeScript file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 126.69,
          "en": "It reports as line four because in the end everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 126.69,
          "end": 129.57,
          "en": "gets merged together and rebuilt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 129.57,
          "end": 132.24,
          "en": "So that is what probably decode then is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 132.24,
          "end": 135.87,
          "en": "in line four in the final code, but not in our code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 138.42000000000002,
          "en": "Still, we got one important clue here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 138.42000000000002,
          "end": 141.06,
          "en": "property push of undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 141.06,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "So we try to call push on something which is not defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 147.3,
          "en": "at the point of time we do call it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 149.04,
          "en": "So if we have a look at our code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 149.04,
          "end": 152.43,
          "en": "we see that there's only one place where we call push",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 152.43,
          "end": 155.61,
          "en": "and that is of course here in the on or add server method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 155.61,
          "end": 157.77,
          "en": "which makes sense because this is the method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 157.77,
          "end": 159.99,
          "en": "which gets triggered once we click the button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 159.99,
          "end": 162.81,
          "en": "So that would've been another way of finding where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 162.81,
          "end": 165.45,
          "en": "the problematic code has to be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 165.45,
          "end": 168.12,
          "en": "As this error occurred when we click the button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 168.12,
          "end": 170.22,
          "en": "it probably is somewhere in the method which is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 171.93,
          "en": "then executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 171.93,
          "end": 175.68,
          "en": "So here, there's something wrong with pushing though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 175.68,
          "end": 177.51,
          "en": "not with pushing itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 177.51,
          "end": 181.47,
          "en": "Remember it said, \"Push of undefined.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 181.47,
          "end": 184.86,
          "en": "So the thing we're calling push on is undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 184.86,
          "end": 187.38,
          "en": "So that would be this servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 187.38,
          "end": 190.14,
          "en": "How can this service be undefined?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 190.14,
          "end": 192.81,
          "en": "We do declare it up here, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 192.81,
          "end": 195,
          "en": "That's exactly the issue in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 198.3,
          "en": "We do declare it here, but we don't define it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 198.3,
          "end": 201.3,
          "en": "We tell TypeScript there's going to be a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 201.3,
          "end": 203.97,
          "en": "called servers, but we don't initialize it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 203.97,
          "end": 206.13,
          "en": "It doesn't have any value assigned to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 206.13,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "It's not an MT array, it's not a string, it's nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 213.72,
          "en": "So to fix our code, we simply have to make sure that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 213.72,
          "end": 218.72,
          "en": "before trying to push a new item on servers, we set servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 218.79,
          "end": 221.25,
          "en": "to an array because otherwise it could be anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 221.25,
          "end": 222.57,
          "en": "It's undefined in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 222.57,
          "end": 225.57,
          "en": "So pushing is not as supported here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 225.57,
          "end": 227.67000000000002,
          "en": "So what we can do is we can simply initialize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 227.67000000000002,
          "end": 229.38,
          "en": "an MT array here at the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 229.38,
          "end": 231.48,
          "en": "And with this little change in place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 231.48,
          "end": 233.04,
          "en": "this should now work as expected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 233.04,
          "end": 235.17000000000002,
          "en": "Once it reloads and we click add server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 235.17000000000002,
          "end": 238.59,
          "en": "now we can add our servers to this list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 238.59,
          "end": 243.15,
          "en": "So this was a brief example for a potential error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 243.15,
          "end": 244.02,
          "en": "how to read it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 244.02,
          "end": 247.77,
          "en": "and how to try to get to the root of the error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 247.77,
          "end": 248.94,
          "en": "Now of course, it's impossible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 248.94,
          "end": 251.13,
          "en": "for me to show all possible error messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 251.13,
          "end": 253.98,
          "en": "and what can go wrong and there are some more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 253.98,
          "end": 257.79,
          "en": "tricky error messages, but it's always great to not panic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 257.79,
          "end": 259.29,
          "en": "but have a look at the message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 259.29,
          "end": 263.22,
          "en": "read which file it points to, read the exact message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 263.22,
          "end": 265.29,
          "en": "There are even error messages in Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 265.29,
          "end": 268.74,
          "en": "which are much clearer than the one I just showed you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 268.74,
          "end": 271.53,
          "en": "And with that, you should be able to narrow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 271.53,
          "end": 273.903,
          "en": "down the issue and hopefully solve it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
